{"shortDescription":"Basis bids for soybeans were steady to weak in the US Midwest on Thursday, softening at some crushing facilities as dry weather promoted an active harvest pace that steered fresh soybean supplies to elevators and processors, dealers said.Basis values are quoted against CBOT futures in cents/bu:NOTE…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Basis bids for soybeans were steady to weak in the US Midwest on Thursday, softening at some crushing facilities as dry weather promoted an active harvest pace that steered fresh soybean supplies to elevators and processors, dealers said."]},{"type":"list","children":[{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The bean basis softened by 5 cents a bushel at crushing plants in Des Moines and Sioux City, Iowa. The two locations, like several others in the region, have scaled back huge premiums that had been offered for soybeans delivered in late September and early October, when rains delayed the harvest."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Corn basis bids were unchanged, spot checks showed."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Some farmers have waited to harvest corn, limiting the influx of fresh corn supplies to grain handlers."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["On the Chicago Board of Trade, soybean and corn futures declined on seasonal pressure from the advancing harvest and position-squaring ahead of monthly supply/demand reports due from the US Department of Agriculture on Friday."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["CBOT November soybean futures (SX26) settled down 10 cents at $12.87-1/2 per bushel and December corn (CZ26) ended down 1-3/4 cents at $5.00-1/4 a bushel."]}]},{"type":"*","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Ahead of Friday's monthly reports, analysts surveyed by Reuters on average expected the USDA to lower its estimate of the US 2026 corn yield to 177.7 bushels per acre, from 178.5 bpa p